  "body": "**Batch gate on upstream/main a5d1a763: one red test.** `camcraft-cl` `tests/headless_bin.rs::cl_text_round_trips_every_golden` fails on `crates/app/tests/golden/sinker_rough_finish_pair.cl`. Everything else is green.\n\n**Cause:** #1136 (merged ebaceb1c) added `sinker_undersize.rs`, which writes the rough and finish CL texts concatenated into ONE golden file, so the file has two `; HSMW-CL` headers. The CL text reader merges both into one 6-move path, and re-serialising gives one header, so the round-trip check fails. Not wrong output: a test-fixture shape problem.\n\n**Done means:** the pair is written as two goldens (`sinker_rough_finish_pair_rough.cl` and `..._finish.cl`), each one CL stream, the old file is removed, and `cl_text_round_trips_every_golden` plus `sinker_undersize` pass.\n",
